From: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 11:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: align MLO peer assoc ABI with current firmware

WLAN.WBE.1.6 firmware is paired with the extended
WMI_MLO_PEER_ASSOC_PARAMS layout used by Qualcomm's current TIP driver.
The extension was introduced together with station link reconfiguration,
but the structure size itself is part of the firmware ABI even when none
of the optional reconfiguration fields are used.

Append the missing fields so the TLV has the layout expected by this
firmware generation.  ath12k_wmi_alloc_skb() zeroes the command buffer,
therefore the newly added optional capabilities remain disabled and this
does not advertise link reconfiguration support.

Signed-off-by: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.h | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.h
@@ -4005,6 +4005,16 @@ struct wmi_peer_assoc_mlo_params {
 	__le32 emlsr_trans_timeout_us;
 	__le32 emlsr_trans_delay_us;
 	__le32 emlsr_padding_delay_us;
+	__le32 msd_dur_subfield;
+	__le32 msd_ofdm_ed_thr;
+	__le32 msd_max_num_txops;
+	__le32 max_num_simultaneous_links;
+	__le32 nstr_indication_bitmap;
+	__le32 recommended_max_num_simultaneous_links;
+	struct {
+		__le32 ml_reconfig: 1,
+		       unused: 31;
+	};
 } __packed;
 
 struct wmi_peer_assoc_complete_cmd {
